{"answer": "The fixture at apps/api/test/fixtures/escalationTriggers.ts is a `Record` over `EscalationTrigger`, checked through a `satisfies` clause, for two reasons. A member added without an entry fails `npm run typecheck` in the same way it would with a no-`default` switch, so the exhaustiveness guarantee is the same. A switch with a case for every member would also exceed the lint complexity limit. The spec's FR-003 originally described the switch. The Record is how it was built, and it has been typechecked since #275.", "sources": ["specs/support-agent-escalation/spec.md (FR-003)", "issue-24", "issue-178", "#275"]}
